### Objective

The objective was to configure the fraud-detector repository so that every pull request automatically executes a machine learning pipeline and registers the resulting model in MLflow.

The platform team required that sensitive configuration values, including the MLflow tracking URI and token, should not be stored in plaintext inside the workflow YAML file.

The implementation uses Gitea repository-level Actions secrets to securely supply these values to the model registration job.

